  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> denote the greatest integer function and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>max</mi><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>,&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is not continuous and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> be the number of points in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is not differentiable. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math> is equal to&nbsp;"
  },
